      "entity": "GPS coverage",
      "classification": "calibration_limitation",
      "reason": "The LMU .duckdb telemetry stores GPS coordinates (Latitude/Longitude) in a separate column table, not directly derivable from the Lap Dist coordinate system. The profile's lap_length_m and all turn boundaries are calibrated from Lap Dist, not from GPS path distance. GPS coordinates are available (coverage 1.0 across all 5 complete laps from 3 independent sessions) and confirm the track geometry is reliable, but the profile does not use GPS-derived distance because Lap Dist is the authoritative distance coordinate for the LMU telemetry format. gps_coverage_derivable = false means Lap Dist cannot be reconstructed from GPS alone; this is a known limitation of the LMU telemetry format and does not affect the profile's validity.",
